cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "3D Road Geometry Coupling"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A modular, open-source C++ library that couples any planar vehicle dynamics model with
  3D road geometry without modifying the planar model itself. Sitting between a 2D
  vehicle model and the 3D world, it transforms the vehicle's planar pose into its 3D
  pose on the actual road surface, lifts the planar measurements into 3D space, and
  computes the road-geometry-induced forces and moments that a planar model would
  otherwise miss. This keeps simpler planar models applicable on banked, sloped, and
  elevated tracks, including high-speed ovals such as the Las Vegas Motor Speedway. The
  core library is independent of ROS 2; Python bindings and ROS 2 nodes are provided
  alongside it.
